# Frontend React Component Testing Best Practices

## createDriver Pattern

**Zero time creating drivers - one line of code:**

```typescript
import { createDataHooks, createDriver } from "@/lib/testing";

// 1. Define hooks
const FORM_HOOKS = createDataHooks(
  "my-form",
  "nameInput",
  "emailInput",
  "submitBtn"
);

// 2. Create driver (one line!)
const myFormDriver = createDriver(FORM_HOOKS);

// 3. Use in test
it("should submit form", async () => {
  const { container } = render(<MyForm />);
  const form = myFormDriver(container);

  await form.nameInput.setText("John");
  await form.emailInput.setText("john@example.com");
  await form.submitBtn.click();

  expect(form.error.exists()).toBe(false);
});
```

**With extensions for complex logic:**

```typescript
const modalDriver = createDriver(MODAL_HOOKS, (driver) => ({
  isOpen: () => driver.content.exists(),
  open: async () => {
    if (!driver.content.exists()) await driver.trigger.click();
  },
}));

const modal = modalDriver(container);
await modal.open();
expect(modal.isOpen()).toBe(true);
```

## Class Wrapper Pattern (For complex cases with mocks)

Use when you need mock setup, complex assertions, or get/when/then structure:

```typescript
import { createDataHooks, createDriver, byDataHook } from "@/lib/testing";

// Base driver with extensions
const myDriver = createDriver(MY_HOOKS, (driver) => ({
  tick: async () => {
    await act(async () => {
      await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 0));
    });
  },
  isToggleChecked: () =>
    driver.toggle.get<HTMLInputElement>()?.checked ?? false,
}));

// Class wrapper for mocks and complex setup
export class MyComponentDriver {
  private container?: HTMLElement;
  private driver?: ReturnType<typeof myDriver>;
  public readonly apiSpy = jest.fn();

  public create(props = {}) {
    jest.clearAllMocks();
    this.setupMocks();
    const result = render(<MyComponent {...props} />);
    this.container = result.container;
    this.driver = myDriver(this.container);
    return result;
  }

  private d() {
    return this.driver!;
  }

  public get = { toggle: () => this.d().toggle.get<HTMLButtonElement>() };

  public when = {
    clickToggle: async () => {
      await this.d().toggle.click();
      await this.d().tick();
    },
  };

  public then = {
    expectToggleChecked: (checked: boolean) => {
      expect(this.d().isToggleChecked()).toBe(checked);
    },
  };
}
```

## File Structure

```
ComponentName/
├── ComponentName.tsx
├── ComponentName.hooks.ts    # Data hooks
├── ComponentName.driver.tsx  # Driver
├── ComponentName.test.tsx    # Tests
└── index.ts
```

## Key Rules

### 1. Use `data-hook` for element selection

```tsx
// Use camelCase for hook keys (enables dot notation in driver)
const HOOKS = createDataHooks("my-form", "submitBtn", "ipInput"); // ✅ camelCase
// NOT: createDataHooks('my-form', 'submit-btn', 'ip-input');      // ❌ requires bracket notation

// In component - root element MUST have component hook:
<div data-hook={HOOKS.component}>
  <Button data-hook={HOOKS.submitBtn}>Submit</Button>
</div>;

// In driver:
const driver = createDriver(HOOKS);
await driver.submitBtn.click(); // Clean dot notation
```

### 2. Use generics for element-specific properties

```typescript
driver.toggle.get<HTMLInputElement>()?.checked;
driver.button.get<HTMLButtonElement>()?.disabled;
driver.input.get<HTMLInputElement>()?.value;
```

### 3. Prefer Testkits for portal components

```typescript
import { selectTestkit } from "@/components/ui-ts/select/select.testkit";

await driver.get.mySelect().selectOption("value");
```

### 4. Handle portaled elements (dialogs, modals)

Portaled elements render outside component root. Query document directly:

```typescript
const myDriver = createDriver(HOOKS, (driver) => ({
  isDialogOpen: () => document.querySelector(byDataHook(HOOKS.dialog)) !== null,

  // ConfirmDialog auto-generates -confirm/-cancel suffixes
  clickDialogConfirm: async () => {
    const btn = document.querySelector(byDataHook(`${HOOKS.dialog}-confirm`));
    if (!btn) throw new Error("Button not found");
    await act(async () => {
      fireEvent.click(btn);
    });
  },
}));
```

## ActionableElementDriver API

| Method                       | Description                                 |
| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| `get<T>()`                   | Get raw element (generic for specific type) |
| `exists()`                   | Check if in DOM                             |
| `getText()`                  | Get text content                            |
| `hasAttribute(attr, value?)` | Check attribute                             |
| `getItem(hook)`              | Get first child by data-hook               |
| `getAllItems(hook)`          | Get all children by data-hook as array     |
| `getItemByIndex(hook, i)`    | Get child by data-hook at index            |
| `click()`                    | Click (RTL handles act internally)          |
| `setText(value)`             | Set input value (RTL handles act internally)|

